{"event": "report", "t": 1795198065.993, "claim": "fixed", "verdict": {"verdict": "fixed", "root_cause": {"category": "logic", "model": "rpt_category_performance", "summary": "The model drives from products and LEFT JOINs down to orders. Order lines with no matching order header (18 ORPHAN-ORD lines, 2,950.78 revenue) and products with no sales therefore land in a NULL sales_month group, which inflates unique_products with products that never sold and puts unattributable revenue in a non-month bucket. Making the orders join inner keeps only lines with a valid order date."}, "evidence": [{"kind": "query", "ref": "stg_orders__order_lines vs stg_orders__orders", "finding": "18 order lines have order_id values (ORPHAN-ORD-*) with no matching row in stg_orders__orders; total line_total 2,950.78, all under PHYSICAL products."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "products LEFT JOIN variants/lines/orders where ordered_at is null", "finding": "Null-month group had PHYSICAL 132 products (18 lines), DIGITAL 8, SERVICE 6, GIFT_CARD 2 products with no sales; these inflated unique_products in NULL-month rows."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "source reconciliation", "finding": "Source line_total sum 722,313.24 equals the report revenue sum before the fix; after the fix it is 719,362.46 = source minus the orphan lines. Units 6,590 -> 6,559 (orphan units removed). No null sales_month rows remain."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "uniqueness checks", "finding": "stg_product__products, stg_product__product_variants, stg_orders__order_lines and stg_orders__orders are unique on their keys, so the join chain does not fan out."}, {"kind": "log", "ref": "run_dbt rpt_category_performance+", "finding": "Build succeeded (1 node, success=1)."}], "changes": [{"path": "models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql", "summary": "Changed the orders join from LEFT JOIN to inner JOIN so only order lines with a valid order header (and therefore a sales_month) are counted. Removes the NULL sales_month bucket and the products with no sales that inflated unique_products. Output columns, grain and materialization are unchanged."}], "confidence": "medium"}, "diffs": [{"path": "models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql", "diff": "--- a/models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql\n+++ b/models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql\n@@ -29,5 +29,5 @@\n from products p\n left join product_variants pv on p.product_id = pv.product_id\n left join order_lines ol on pv.variant_id = ol.variant_id\n-left join orders o on ol.order_id = o.order_id\n+join orders o on ol.order_id = o.order_id\n group by 1, 2\n"}], "text": "The verifier accepted the fix for `rpt_category_performance`, and the run is closed.\n\n**Root cause:** The model starts from products and left-joins down to order lines and orders. That produced two problems:\n- 18 order lines reference order IDs (`ORPHAN-ORD-*`) that don't exist in `stg_orders__orders`. Their 2,950.78 of revenue fell into a NULL `sales_month` group.\n- Products with no sales also landed in that NULL group, which inflated `unique_products`.\n\n**Fix:** I changed the orders join from `left join` to `join` in `models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql`. Only lines with a valid order header and date now count. Output columns, grain and materialization are unchanged.\n\n**Checks:**\n- Revenue went from 722,313.24 (the full source total) to 719,362.46, which is the source minus exactly the orphan lines.\n- Units went from 6,590 to 6,559, which is the orphan units removed.\n- No NULL `sales_month` rows remain.\n- The four source tables are unique on their keys, so the join chain doesn't fan out.\n- `run_dbt` on `rpt_category_performance+` succeeded.\n\n**Confidence is medium.** Dropping the orphan lines is a judgment call: they have no order header, so they can't be dated. The project's `dq_orphaned_records` model tracks that kind of row, which supports excluding them from the report. The verifier passed the fix, but it can't confirm that dropping those rows is the intended business treatment.\n\n**Not addressed:**\n- The full `dbt build` still shows many unrelated test failures in staging models, and a `product_categories` seed error from a name clash with the existing `PRODUCT_CATEGORIES` table. I left them alone because they are outside this model.\n- The report's `category` column is `product_type` (DIGITAL, GIFT_CARD, PHYSICAL, SERVICE), not the product category hierarchy. I did not change this, because the task asked for a repair, not a change of grouping."}
